{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /local/home/scheschb/.codex/plugins/cache/aim/AmazonBuilderCoreAIAgents-core/1.0.6505391367/skills/brazil/references/language/rust.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /local/home/scheschb/.codex/plugins/cache/aim/AmazonBuilderCoreAIAgents-core/1.0.6505391367/skills/brazil/references/language/rust.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Rust with CargoBrazil\n\nCargoBrazil integrates Rust with Amazon's Brazil build system, managing toolchains and dependencies while preserving standard Cargo workflows.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Create a New Rust Package\n\nUse CreateHub to generate from template:\n```bash\n# Via toolbox\ntoolbox install create-pkg\ncreate-pkg --template DuplicatorRustPackage --name MyPackage\n\n# Or via CreateHub web UI\n# https://createhub.corp.amazon.com/templates/DuplicatorRustPackage\n```\n\nThis creates a properly configured package with Config, Cargo.toml, and .gitignore already set up.\n\n### Essential .gitignore\n\n```gitignore\n# Generated by CargoBrazil - never commit\nCargo.lock\n/build\ntarget/\n/rust-toolchain.toml\n\n# IDE artifacts\n.idea/\n*.iml\n```\n\n### First Build\n\n```bash\nbrazil ws create --root --vs YourVersionSet\ncd src/YourPackage\nbrazil-build sync      # Setup (run after clone or metadata changes)\nbrazil-build release   # Full build: tests + lints + docs\n```\n\nAfter first build, standard `cargo` commands work directly:\n```bash\ncargo build            # Fast iteration\ncargo test             # Run tests\ncargo clippy           # Linting\ncargo fmt              # Format code\n```\n\n## Workspace Structure\n\n### Single Crate Package\n\n```\nMyPackage/\n├── Config             # Brazil configuration\n├── Cargo.toml         # Rust manifest\n├── src/\n│   └── lib.rs         # or main.rs for binary\n└── build-tools/bin/   # Optional: build scripts\n```\n\n### Multi-Crate Workspace\n\n```\nMyPackage/\n├── Config\n├── Cargo.toml         # Workspace manifest\n├── crates/\n│   ├── core/\n│   │   ├── Cargo.toml\n│   │   └── src/\n│   └── cli/\n│       ├── Cargo.toml\n│       └── src/\n└── build-tools/bin/\n```\n\nWorkspace Cargo.toml:\n```toml\n[workspace]\nresolver = \"2\"\nmembers = [\"crates/*\"]\n\n[workspace.package]\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[workspace.dependencies]\n# Shared dependencies with versions\nserde = { version = \"1.0\", features = [\"derive\"] }\ntokio = { version = \"1.0\", features = [\"full\"] }\n```\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Third-Party (crates.io)\n\nAdd directly to `Cargo.toml` - no Config or BTPT needed:\n```toml\n[dependencies]\nserde = { version = \"1.0\", features = [\"derive\"] }\ntokio = { version = \"1.0\", features = [\"full\"] }\nanyhow = \"1.0\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nmockall = \"0.11\"\nproptest = \"1.0\"\n```\n\nDependencies come from internal mirror (ThirdPartyCratesIoIndex), which typically lags 1-3 days behind crates.io.\n\n### First-Party (Amazon packages)\n\n1. Add to Config:\n```\ndependencies = {\n    1.0 = {\n        SomeRustPackage = 1.x;\n    };\n};\n```\n\n2. Reference in Cargo.toml with `amzn-` prefix:\n```toml\n[dependencies]\namzn-some-crate = \"*\"  # Version from Config/version set\n```\n\n**Important:** The `amzn-` prefix is mandatory. CargoBrazil maps this to the actual crate name from the version set.\n\n### Native Libraries\n\nFor C/C++ dependencies (OpenSSL, zlib, etc.):\n\n```\ndependencies = {\n    1.0 = {\n        Openssl = default;\n        Zlib = 1.x;\n    };\n};\n```\n\nCargoBrazil automatically:\n- Sets `PKG_CONFIG_PATH` for discovery\n- Configures linker search paths\n- Sets library-specific env vars (`OPENSSL_LIB_DIR`, `OPENSSL_INCLUDE_DIR`)\n\n**Twisted builds error:**\n```\nDenying call to cc due to possible silent vendoring in crate '<crate>'\n```\n\n**Fix:** The crate is compiling C code instead of using Brazil's library. Add the corresponding native library to your Config dependencies:\n- `openssl-sys` → add `Openssl = default`\n- `curl-sys` → add `Curl = 7.x`\n- `bzip2-sys` → add `Bzip2 = 1.0`\n\n**Not your direct dependency?** Try `brazil ws sync --md` - an upstream library may have fixed it.\n\nFull guide: https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/Rust/Campaigns/TwistedBuilds/\n\n## Publishing a Library\n\nTo make your crate consumable by other packages:\n\n### Step 1: Add Target\n\n```\ntargets = {\n    MyPackage-1.0 = { type = rust; };\n};\n```\n\n### Step 2: Configure Cargo.toml\n\n```toml\n[package]\nname = \"amzn-mypackage\"  # Must use amzn- prefix\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\npublish = [\"brazil\"]\nexclude = ['/build', '/Config', '/build-tools/']\n\n[lib]\nname = \"amzn_mypackage\"  # Underscores for Rust identifier\n```\n\n### Step 3: Verify\n\nAfter building, consumers can add to their Cargo.toml:\n```toml\n[dependencies]\namzn-mypackage = \"*\"\n```\n\n## Common Tasks\n\n### Adding Build Tools\n\nCommon tools to add to your Config `build-tools` section:\n\n**For faster builds:**\n- `Mold = 2.x` - Faster linking (Linux, ~2-5x speedup)\n- `Cargo-nextest = 0.x` - Faster parallel test execution\n\n**For code quality:**\n- `Grcov = 0.8.x` - Test coverage reporting\n\n**Example config:**\n```\nbuild-tools = {\n    0.1 = {\n        CargoBrazil = 1.0;\n        RustLang1x = 1.x;\n        Grcov = 0.8.x;\n        Cargo-nextest = 0.x;\n        Mold = 2.x;\n    };\n};\n```\n\n**Security scanning and unused dependency detection** require additional setup beyond build-tools. See https://w.amazon.com/bin/view/Rust/AuditingDependencies for CargoEevee and cargo-machete configuration.\n\n### Test Coverage\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Add `Grcov = 0.8.x` to build-tools\n2. Run coverage:\n\n```bash\ncargo brazil with-coverage test --workspace  # Run instrumented tests\ncargo brazil with-coverage report            # Generate HTML report\n# Report at: build/private/cargo-target/coverage/\n```\n\n**Require minimum coverage:**\n```toml\n# Cargo.toml\n[package.metadata.cargobrazil]\nmin-line-coverage = 80\n```\n\nBuild fails if coverage drops below threshold.\n\n### Compiler Flags\n\nUse `.cargo/config.toml` (NOT the RUSTFLAGS env var, which CargoBrazil manages):\n\n```toml\n[build]\nrustflags = [\"-C\", \"target-feature=+crt-static\"]\n\n# For specific targets\n[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-musl]\nrustflags = [\"-C\", \"target-feature=+crt-static\"]\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
